I now have a comprehensive picture of the current owner identity implementation. Here is my report.

## Summary

The codebase is Spring PetClinic REST with an OfficeFloor-based function pipeline for `POST /api/owners`. Note: `src/test/.../acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` already encodes a **planned redesign** — its one test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` asserts `customerCode` must match `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` (i.e. `<REGION>-<HASH8>`), which the current implementation does NOT satisfy (current format is `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`). Relevant test helpers (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`, region tables) already exist in `AcceptanceBase`.

